      "reasoning": "Looking at my starting hand:\n\
\n\
**Cards in hand:**\n\
1. Delighted Halfling ({G}) - 1/2 with mana abilities for legendary spells\n\
2. Dredger's Insight ({1}{G}) - mills 4, lets me grab a card from grave\n\
3. Formidable Speaker ({2}{G}) - 2/4 that can search for creatures\n\
4. Misty Rainforest (land)\n\
5. Overgrown Tomb (land)\n\
6. Verdant Catacombs (land)\n\
7. Yawgmoth, Thran Physician ({2}{B}{B}) - 2/4 with sacrifice/proliferate\n\
\n\
**Evaluation:**\n\
- Only 3 lands in a 7-card hand is below curve\n\
- Yawgmoth costs {2}{B}{B} which is hard to cast with only Overgrown Tomb providing black\n\
- Dredger's Insight and Formidable Speaker need specific conditions to shine\n\
- The hand lacks early game impact and card advantage\n\
- Three fetch lands are nice but don't help cast spells\n\
\n\
This is a keepable hand but on the weaker side. I'll **MULLIGAN** to look for 4+ lands in my opening hand and better early-game plays.\n\
