- The two Fatal Pushes are flexible removal that we can cast early\n\
- Faithless Looting can help us dig and potentially discard cards\n\
- Unearth is still dead without creatures\n\
- Bloodstained Mire and Watery Grave are lands\n\
\n\
If we keep Abhorrent Oculus, we're keeping a card we can't realistically cast until we've filled our graveyard, which could take many turns. The Fatal Pushes, Looting, and Unearth all cost 1 mana, so they're much more flexible.\n\
\n\
I think we should put Abhorrent Oculus on the bottom to improve our chances of finding a creature or more early plays. Getting that 5-drop off the bottom will give us better access to our early-game cards that can actually impact the game right away.\n\
