  - Faithless Looting\n\
  - Two Fatal Pushes\n\
  - Unearth\n\
\n\
We need to decide which land to play first.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
1. Bloodstained Mire: Pay 1 life, sacrifice to search for a Mountain or Swamp. This would give us another land fixing, but costs life.\n\
2. Watery Grave: Pay 2 life or it enters tapped. Can add U or B.\n\
\n\
Since we have Emperor of Bones in hand, which costs {2}{B}, we want to have black mana available. Watery Grave can produce black mana immediately when entering untapped, while we'd need to sacrifice the Mire to search for a land.\n\
\n\
We should play Watery Grave and pay 2 life. This keeps our life total at 18, which is fine for now, and gives us:\n\
- Immediate access to black mana\n\
- The option to fetch a land later with Bloodstained Mire\n\
- Two untapped lands for next turn\n\
\n\
We can play Watery Grave untapped by paying 2 life, then pass.\n\
\n\
The Mire can be used later to fetch a Swamp or potentially a dual land if needed for fixing.\n\
\n\
This play maximizes our mana efficiency and keeps options open.\n\
\n\
\n\
