      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "We're at the start of turn 3. Our board state:\n\
- Emperor of Bones (2/2, no summoning sickness)\n\
- Watery Grave (untapped)\n\
- Swamp (untapped)\n\
- Hand: Faithless Looting, Fatal Push, Scalding Tarn, Unearth x2\n\
\n\
Opponent's board:\n\
- Badgermole Cub (2/2)\n\
- Swamp creature (1/1 with haste)\n\
- Spymaster's Vault\n\
- Overgrown Tomb  \n\
- Eldrazi Spawn token (0/1, created this turn)\n\
- Several lands in graveyard\n\
\n\
We have 2 black mana available, and can play a land.\n\
\n\
Our best play is to play Scalding Tarn and potentially sacrifice it to search for another land. \n\
But what should we search for? Our deck seems to want Swamps (to power Spymaster's Vault effect, though we don't have one), and we already have 3 black sources. \n\
\n\
Looking at our options, we have Faithless Looting in hand which requires red - but we don't have any red sources. We should probably get a source of red.\n\
\n\
Scalding Tarn can get Island or Mountain. A Mountain would give us red mana.\n\
\n\
Playing Scalding Tarn and sacrificing it for a Mountain would:\n\
- Give us access to red mana for Faithless Looting\n\
- Improve our mana base\n\
- Put another land in the graveyard (good for potential effects)\n\
- Cost us 1 life (from 17 to 16, acceptable)\n\
\n\
After playing the Mountain, we'll have 3 lands that can tap for mana, with one Mountain giving us red.\n\
\n\
Let's do that sequence:\n\
\n\
1. Play Scalding Tarn\n\
2. Sacrifice it to search for a Mountain\n\
3. We'll then have the option to cast Faithless Looting (if we want)\n\
\n\
I'll start by playing Scalding Tarn:\n\
\n\
