- Archon of Cruelty (6BB) - still too expensive (need 5 lands)\n\
- Psychic Frog ({U}{B}) - card draw engine\n\
- Ragavan ({R}) - early pressure\n\
- Thoughtseize ({B}) - hand disruption\n\
- Unearth ({B}) - recursion\n\
- Faithless Looting ({R}) - card selection\n\
\n\
We now have Emperor at 3/3 again after previous combat.\n\
\n\
We're in a position where we can start building toward casting Archon of Cruelty next turn.\n\
\n\
Best play:\n\
- Cast **Psychic Frog** ({U}{B})\n\
\n\
Why?\n\
- It's only 2 mana\n\
- Provides a card draw engine: whenever it deals combat damage, we draw\n\
- Can get flying later by exiling 3 from GY\n\
- Enables us to dig for more cards\n\
- Builds toward a powerful board with Archon coming\n\
\n\
We could grow Emperor, but it's better to accelerate our hand with Psychic Frog.\n\
\n\
I'll cast Psychic Frog:\n\
