\n\
We need to respond.\n\
\n\
Let’s evaluate:\n\
\n\
- **Emperor of Bones (p35)** is currently **2/2 with summoning sickness**, so it can't block or attack.\n\
- We have **Fatal Push (p26)** in hand, which can destroy a creature with mana value ≤2 (or ≤4 with Revolt).\n\
- **Yawgmoth, Thran Physician** has **mana value 3**, so **Fatal Push cannot kill it** unless we have Revolt.\n\
- Did a permanent leave the battlefield under our control this turn?  \n\
  Yes — we attacked with Emperor of Bones, but no creatures died or were sacrificed yet. So **no Revolt**, meaning Fatal Push **cannot** target Yawgmoth.\n\
\n\
So: **we cannot kill Yawgmoth this turn**.\n\
\n\
Also, **Unearth (p16, p43)** could return a creature from our graveyard, but since it's on the stack as a response, timing is tight.\n\
\n\
But — right now, the **only action pending** is **targeting for Yawgmoth's ability**: we must choose a card from a graveyard (up to one), or pass.\n\
\n\
We control:\n\
- **Emperor of Bones**, which exiles cards from graveyards.\n\
- We have **Archon of Cruelty** in hand and in graveyard.\n\
- Opponent used Yawgmoth’s ability — **who controls the ability?** It’s on the stack from the *opponent*, so **we are choosing a target for *their* ability**.\n\
\n\
Wait — this is **our turn**, during **begin_combat**, and **opponent is using Yawgmoth’s ability** to put a -1/-1 counter on our Emperor.\n\
\n\
So the stack is:\n\
- Opponent activated: **Pay 1 life, sacrifice another creature → put -1/-1 counter on target creature and draw a card**\n\
- Targeting our Emperor\n\
- Now we must **choose a target for *that* ability**? No.\n\
\n\
Wait — re-read:  \n\
\"Select up to one card from a graveyard\" — that’s **our part of the resolution**? No.\n\
\n\
Actually, no — **Yawgmoth’s ability** has two parts:\n\
1. Pay 1 life, sacrifice another creature\n\
2. Put -1/-1 counter on up to one target creature and draw a card\n\
\n\
But here, the **opponent sacrificed a creature already** (likely a token or something), paid life, and now the **\"put -1/-1 and draw\"** is on the stack, targeting our Emperor.\n\
\n\
But the **\"select up to one card from a graveyard\"** is being asked of *us*. That doesn't make sense — we don't control the ability.\n\
\n\
Unless… this is *our* ability?\n\
\n\
No — the stack says: `{\"stack\":[{\"name\":\"Ability\"}]}` — no controller specified.\n\
\n\
Look at the battlefield: opponent controls **Yawgmoth, Thran Physician (p36)**, so it’s their ability.\n\
\n\
So why are *we* being asked to choose a card from a graveyard?\n\
\n\
Wait — re-read the ability:  \n\
\"Pay 1 life, Sacrifice another creature: Put a -1/-1 counter on up to one target creature and draw a card.\"\n\
\n\
There is **no graveyard targeting** in that ability.\n\
\n\
But the **prompt** says: \"Select up to one card from a graveyard\"\n\
\n\
This suggests it might be **our own ability** — perhaps **Emperor of Bones**’ beginning of combat trigger?\n\
\n\
But the stack wasn’t showing that.\n\
\n\
Wait — earlier log context (before reset) said Emperor had a -1/-1 counter after combat.\n\
\n\
But now we’re at **begin_combat** of *our* turn — so **beginning of combat** should trigger **Emperor of Bones**’ ability:  \n\
\"At the beginning of combat on your turn, exile up to one target card from a graveyard.\"\n\
\n\
Ah! That’s it.\n\
\n\
So most likely:\n\
- **Emperor of Bones**’ **triggered ability** went on the stack\n\
- We are being asked to **target a card in a graveyard to exile**\n\
\n\
That makes sense.\n\
\n\
So this is **our** ability, not opponent’s.\n\
\n\
Therefore, we must choose a card from any graveyard to exile.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
- Our graveyard: Archon of Cruelty (p123), Bloodstained Mire (p10), Faithless Looting x3, Polluted Delta, Psychic Frog, Ragavan, Scalding Tarn\n\
- Opponent’s graveyard: Badgermole Cub x2, Delighted Halfling x2, Malevolent Rumble x2, Misty Rainforest, Overgrown Tomb, Spymaster’s Vault, Verdant Catacombs x2, Walking Ballista x2, Yawgmoth, Young Wolf\n\
\n\
