      "reasoning": "We're in **declare_blockers** step.\n\
\n\
We have two attackers:\n\
- **Emperor of Bones** (3/3)\n\
- **Young Wolf** (1/1)\n\
\n\
Opponent has:\n\
- **Badgermole Cub** (2/2)\n\
- **Boseiju, Who Endures** (2/2 with haste)\n\
- **Yawgmoth, Thran Physician** (2/4)\n\
- Two Forests, two Dredger’s Insight, Spymaster’s Vault, Swamp\n\
\n\
They can block with **Badgermole Cub** and **Yawgmoth**.\n\
\n\
Possible blocking:\n\
- **Yawgmoth** **(2/4) can block **Emperor **(3/3) — trades, we lose Emperor\n\
- **Badgermole Cub** (2/2) can block **Young Wolf **(1/1) — trade\n\
- **Boseiju** is tapped, but haste ends — likely can't block unless they can untap\n\
\n\
Boseiju had haste, but if it entered this turn, it will still be there, but tapped.\n\
\n\
No way to untap it in combat.\n\
\n\
So only **Badgermole Cub** and **Yawgmoth** can block.\n\
\n\
Likely blocking:\n\
- Yawgmoth blocks Emperor → 3 vs 4 — Emperor dies, Yawgmoth survives at 1 toughness\n\
- Badgermole blocks Young Wolf → 1 vs 2 — Young Wolf dies, Badgermole survives\n\
\n\
Damage:\n\
- Emperor deals 3 → prevented by Yawgmoth\n\
- Young Wolf deals 1 → prevented\n\
- No damage through\n\
\n\
But we have **Unearth** in hand — we could cast **Unearth** during opponent’s declare blockers to return **Ragavan** or **Psychic Frog** to add another attacker.\n\
\n\
But **Unearth** creates a creature that **does not have summoning sickness** — so it can attack.\n\
\n\
And we are **after** declare attackers, but **before** combat damage — opportunity to cast instants.\n\
\n\
So: **cast Unearth now** to return **Ragavan** (2/1, menace) — it enters with haste, can immediately attack? No — only creatures declared as attackers in **declare_attackers** step can attack.\n\
\n\
You cannot add attackers after the step.\n\
\n\
So **Unearth now is too late** for attacking.\n\
\n\
It can block, though.\n\
\n\
But we’re not defending.\n\
\n\
So **no benefit** to casting **Unearth** now.\n\
\n\
Similarly, **Fatal Push** — no target, Yawgmoth is 2/4, mana value 3.\n\
\n\
**Adapt** Emperor again? It already has a +1/+1 counter — Adapt would give two more, making it 5/5, but opponent will likely trade.\n\
\n\
Not worth 2B.\n\
\n\
Best play: **pass**, let combat damage resolve.\n\
\n\
Opponent will likely block as above.\n\
\n\
So:\n\
\n\
