    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Earthbending the Swamp instead of Overgrown Tomb means the animated land only taps for B (one color), whereas Overgrown Tomb taps for B or G. More importantly, the Swamp was just fetched and is a basic — losing it to removal means losing a basic land, while Overgrown Tomb can be recovered the same way (earthbend returns the land tapped when it dies). Additionally, Badgermole Cub's ability adds G when you tap a creature for mana, so animating Overgrown Tomb gives you a creature that can tap for G (getting an additional G from the Cub's triggered ability), providing more mana flexibility. The Swamp as a creature only taps for B with no additional G. With Yawgmoth (BBBB) and green spells in hand, having the dual land as the animated creature that can tap for either color while the basic Swamp stays as a regular land provides better mana development.",
